# .cursorrules - Factory Forge Project Rules for AI Assistants

You are working on Factory Forge, a 2D grid-based factory builder game built with a client-server architecture.

Guidelines:
- Stack: Node.js 22+ (using native node:http, node:sqlite, node:test, node:crypto) on the backend; HTML5 Canvas + Vanilla modern ES modules on the frontend.
- Zero external npm dependencies: Do NOT introduce external npm packages unless strictly instructed.
- All simulation logic in `src/simulation.js` must be deterministic and pure.
- Backpressure & congestion: Conveyors hold max 1 item. When downstream is blocked, upstream machines pause production without losing or duplicating items.
- Offline profit limit: Always capped at 24 hours (86,400 seconds) calculated on the server side using server timestamps.
- Testing: All automated tests live in `tests/` and run using `node --test tests/*.test.js`.
- Always follow the acceptance criteria defined in `spec.md` and agent definitions in `AGENTS.md`.
